AVAILABLE
============================================
!
! FLEXPART v11 'pathnames' — four lines, read in this exact order by readpaths
! (src/readoptions_mod.f90:1861). Everything from the '=====' line down is ignored,
! so these notes are safe to keep.
!
!   line 1  the options directory (COMMAND, RELEASES, OUTGRID, SPECIES/, ...)
!   line 2  the output directory  — FLEXPART does NOT create it; the run script does
!   line 3  the directory holding the GRIB files from flex_extract
!   line 4  the AVAILABLE file
!
! The first three MUST end in '/'. FLEXPART pads a missing one and prints
!   'WARNING: path not ending in /'  ...  'fix: padded with /'
! but a path is truncated at its first blank, so a directory name with a space in it
! silently becomes something else. Avoid spaces.
!
! Line 4 is a file, not a directory: no trailing slash. It may be relative to the
! directory you launch FLEXPART from, like everything else here.
!
! For nested meteorological input, add TWO more lines per nest after the '====='
! separator (nest met directory, then nest AVAILABLE) and move the separator to the
! end — up to maxnests = 5 (par_mod.f90:151).
